  "configuration_id": "config_036",
  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with scvi_n200/multiprofile achieves 0.650–0.653, while the sole multimodal experiment (config_030: scvi_n200, resnet50, avgpool, concat) underperforms at 0.632. Image-only models are very weak (0.208–0.227), suggesting the image modality may be adding noise. Uncertainty: it is unclear whether the multimodal deficit is due to the relatively weak resnet50 image encoder or a fundamental lack of image signal for this task. Question tested: config_036 swaps only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l (the stronger encoder, which was also better in image-only: 0.227 vs 0.208) while holding all other settings identical to config_030. This isolates the effect of image representation quality. Why best next experiment: If even the best available image encoder cannot lift the multimodal model above the RNA-only baseline, we can confidently conclude the image modality is uninformative for this task and redirect remaining budget to RNA-only optimization. If it does help, it reveals that image encoder quality is the bottleneck and justifies further multimodal exploration. This single-variable comparison maximizes information per experiment under the limited budget."
}

